# ntpstat configuration template
#
# NOTE: ntpstat is a diagnostic utility that queries the local system's NTP
# daemon (usually ntpd, chronyd, or systemd-timesyncd) to report its synchronization status.
#
# ntpstat DOES NOT have a configuration file. It reads the status from the running
# NTP daemon's shared memory or control socket.
#
# To configure the NTP source (the server to synchronize with), please configure
# the underlying NTP daemon (e.g., /etc/ntp.conf for ntpd, /etc/chrony.conf for chrony).
#
# This package provides NO configuration directives and requires NO peer injection.
# It is a pure consumer of the NTP daemon's state.

# No configuration directives exist for ntpstat itself.